  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Japanese Social Development Fund (JSDF) Parallel to TF023779</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;Fund amounts may be used to finance Project Grants and Capacity Building Grants
 for the following types of activities:
 (a) Project Grants may be used to finance activities directly providing relief
 measures, improvement of services and facilities for poorer population groups
 or reinforcing social safety nets and innovation and testing of new approaches,
 particularly in the social sectors, which could be replicated on a larger scale or
 included in operations financed by World Bank Group entities.
 (b) Capacity Building Grants may be used to finance the following types of
 activities: capacity building and improvement measures, such as bolstering
 local communities and non-government organizations (NGOs) to facilitate
 their involvement in operations financed by World Bank Group entities
 TO BENEFIT THE MOST FRAGILE AND VULNERABLE GROUPS IN ELIGIBLE COUNTRIES&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
